><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l" indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="560"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2800"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>In bacteria, tightly coupled to transcription</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l" indent="-285750" lvl="1" marL="742950" marR="0" rtl="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="480"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="–"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" cap="none" i="0" lang="en-US" strike="noStrike" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Translation can begin before transcription is finished.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="541" name="Google Shape;541;p75"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="381000" y="838200"/><a:ext cx="8382000" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" type="none" w="med"/><a:tailEnd len="med" type="none" w="med"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="Coupling of transcription and translation in bacteria. 
In image (a) at the top, a purple rectangle with a light blue line running horizontally right and up. On this line are various-shaped black circles bonded outlined in red, labeled as polysomes. These get larger as they travel right. Image (b) has the ovoid RNA polymerase figure, with a double blue DNA chain running through the middle. This line extends down and right, then through another RNA polymerase. The line extends down and right through yet another RNA polymerase. Each of these has a right arrow off the top ovoid indicating the direction of transcription. Each of these also has a green line extending down and left to a small sideways version of the large and small subunit bonded together. In the first one, the subunit has two green elongated intertwines structures, which each have a blue circle. On the left, it has several blue circles extending left, then down. This green line connects down to another subunit image, where the blue circles stop at the top and do not extend down. This line continues down to another subunit, but this one has the large and small subunits separate. The green image is now on the small subunit with a blue circle on top. The large subunit is labeled as 50S and the small subunit is labeled as 30S and the green line ends with 5[prime]. This represents incoming ribosomal subunits. The second RNA polymerase also has the same set of subunits below, but also has another one just above what was the first one on the left. This has an even longer set of blue circles streaming down. The right RNA polymerase has the same 4 structures as to the one in the middle, but at the top, another is added with an even longer set of blue circles streaming down. This set of subunits and the set in the middle are labeled as polysomes. Each of these sets of subunits have arrow pointing up, indicating the direction of translation. 
